{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>For now also you — etc.</b> Its saying <b>now</b> accords with what they, of blessed memory, said (Numbers Rabbah 20:14) — that the she-ass was killed. Therefore he was precise in saying <b>also you</b> and did not say ״I would also have killed you,״ for the word ״now״ must be examined carefully: for it would not be fitting to say ״also you״ except now, after the she-ass had already been killed — which was not so earlier, for earlier the she-ass had not died, as He said: ״I kept her alive.״ And His saying <b>I kept her alive (הֶחֱיֵיתִי)</b> — which has the force of a new action — is meant to alert you that now she was killed. Further, it may be said that a miracle was performed for her: that the angel would encounter both rider and mount, and kill the rider while preserving the mount; and in this manner this expression ״I kept her alive״ is fitting."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:44.419665159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}